   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Primary Grid Split\n\nA primary-colour grid draws itself line by line, fills with primary colors, and one cell expands to take over the frame.\n\nCategory: shapes. Length: 4.85 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A scene change or title should arrive as a primary-colour grid that draws itself and then opens into the next scene.\n- A bold, flat, art-poster look is wanted.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A soft, photographic or minimal transition is needed.\n- You need the color field to match a specific brand palette that is not primary: set the colors explicitly.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"\"\n- seed (number, 1-99): Seed, default 7\n- splits (number, 3-12): Splits, default 7\n- line_weight (number, 4-32): Line weight, default 14\n- expand_cell (number, 0-12): Expanding cell, default 0\n- line_color (color): Lines, default \"#121212\"\n- red_color (color): Red, default \"#d62d20\"\n- yellow_color (color): Yellow, default \"#f4c20d\"\n- blue_color (color): Blue, default \"#1f4e9e\"\n- field_color (color): Expanding cell color, default \"#d62d20\"\n- text_color (color): Text color, default \"#ffffff\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
